WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.144
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:09.414 --> 00:12.050
LIFE INSURANCE

3
00:23.428 --> 00:25.763
People have gone missing on Mount Shikara, Hokkaido.

4
00:26.331 --> 00:28.266
One has died, and two have been rescued.

5
00:28.333 --> 00:30.335
Three remain missing.

6
00:31.136 --> 00:33.004
Ms. Saruwatari. Open your eyes!

7
00:33.071 --> 00:34.139
Ms. Aya!

8
00:34.205 --> 00:35.039
Thank you.

9
00:35.106 --> 00:36.541
You saved my life.

10
00:37.108 --> 00:40.478
According to Aya Saruwatari, Ogoma's middle school teacher…

11
00:40.545 --> 00:41.846
I'll go bring him back.

12
00:41.913 --> 00:43.348
No, I will.

13
00:44.082 --> 00:46.618
Everyone, please don't move for a while.

14
00:47.585 --> 00:48.753
A heat pack.

15
00:49.420 --> 00:50.655
Thank you.

16
00:54.826 --> 00:57.395
The deceased, Teruyuki Nikaido, a restaurant owner,

17
00:57.462 --> 00:59.864
had his wife, Harune, as his beneficiary.

18
00:59.931 --> 01:04.002
She is now suspected of insurance fraud for 150 million yen.

19
01:05.003 --> 01:06.571
ORIENT DINER

20
01:10.775 --> 01:13.845
Police! We're from Kitami HQ!

21
01:15.246 --> 01:16.080
I'm…

22
01:16.147 --> 01:17.715
I'm coming!

23
01:25.356 --> 01:26.391
Hello, officers.

24
01:26.457 --> 01:27.325
Please, excuse us.

25
01:27.392 --> 01:30.495
May we borrow Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido's computer and tablet?

26
01:31.062 --> 01:32.130
Of course.

27
01:34.532 --> 01:36.367
73 HOURS HAVE PASSED

28
01:40.071 --> 01:41.706
Reinforcements from Kitami HQ.

29
01:42.507 --> 01:44.642
-Let's remain calm. -Yes.

30
01:45.677 --> 01:47.011
Hello, sir. This way.

31
01:47.078 --> 01:47.979
Hello.

32
01:48.046 --> 01:49.047
Hello.

33
01:50.415 --> 01:53.184
Thank you all for your help these past few days.

34
01:53.251 --> 01:54.852
Thank you, sir!

35
01:54.919 --> 01:57.555
Let's begin the investigation meeting.

36
01:57.622 --> 02:01.259
Three tour guests are still missing. The search continues.

37
02:01.326 --> 02:04.229
Two people were rescued. The guide, Motoka Tabatake,

38
02:04.295 --> 02:05.863
and the tour guest, Aya Saruwatari.

39
02:05.930 --> 02:10.401
Tabatake had moderate hypothermia but regained consciousness earlier today.

40
02:10.468 --> 02:12.837
We've already questioned Saruwatari.

41
02:12.904 --> 02:16.107
The body found was Teruyuki Nikaido, 44.

42
02:16.174 --> 02:18.176
The cause of death was brain injury from a fall.

43
02:18.243 --> 02:22.714
The autopsy found the sleeping pill Zolpidem in his blood.

44
02:22.780 --> 02:26.651
He took it between 1:00 p.m. and 2:00 p.m. on the day they went missing.

45
02:26.718 --> 02:28.653
He carried no medicine.

46
02:28.720 --> 02:31.923
We suspect someone made him take it somehow.

47
02:32.590 --> 02:33.891
Any possible motives?

48
02:33.958 --> 02:34.959
Yes!

49
02:35.493 --> 02:38.763
Nikaido had 150 million yen in life insurance.

50
02:38.830 --> 02:42.200
It was 50 million at first, but was increased two months ago.

51
02:42.267 --> 02:44.369
The beneficiary is his wife, Harune.

52
02:44.435 --> 02:48.306
Right after the body was found, she asked the insurance company about the claim.

53
02:48.373 --> 02:50.375
She cared about money more than her husband.

54
02:50.908 --> 02:52.410
One more point of suspicion.

55
02:52.977 --> 02:55.613
All the tour guests had hiking insurance.

56
02:55.680 --> 02:58.149
The beneficiary upon their death is…

57
02:58.950 --> 03:00.251
Saruwatari.

58
03:00.885 --> 03:02.287
Even for Nikaido?

59
03:02.353 --> 03:04.822
For all four, the three missing and Nikaido.

60
03:04.889 --> 03:07.592
-20 million in total-- -I spoke to the insurance company!

61
03:08.259 --> 03:12.163
To receive the money, Saruwatari needs the guests' consent and signatures.

62
03:12.230 --> 03:13.665
There are no signatures,

63
03:13.731 --> 03:16.734
so it's practically impossible for her to get the 20 million yen.

64
03:16.801 --> 03:19.971
Maybe she didn’t know and tried anyway.

65
03:20.038 --> 03:23.274
The person who handled the hiking insurance was Tabatake.

66
03:24.175 --> 03:25.009
Thank you.

67
03:25.843 --> 03:29.947
Guests can't see or change other guests' applications.

68
03:30.915 --> 03:33.918
The only one who can is Tabatake.

69
03:37.755 --> 03:40.558
Does Tabatake or Saruwatari have any connection to Nikaido’s wife?

70
03:40.625 --> 03:42.593
We're checking their relationships.

71
03:42.660 --> 03:43.628
Yes.

72
03:45.129 --> 03:46.097
Hello.

73
03:46.164 --> 03:46.998
Hello.

74
03:47.065 --> 03:48.466
Did Ms. Saruwatari's surgery go well?

75
03:48.533 --> 03:50.134
It went well.

76
03:50.201 --> 03:51.436
Do you have time now?

77
03:51.502 --> 03:52.737
Do I look like I do?

78
03:52.804 --> 03:54.472
I checked the hiking insurance.

79
03:54.539 --> 03:56.474
I checked too.

80
03:56.541 --> 03:57.642
Really?

81
03:58.242 --> 04:00.278
What’s with that smug look?

82
04:00.345 --> 04:03.614
Ms. Saruwatari gets twenty million yen.

83
04:04.248 --> 04:05.116
Huh?

84
04:05.183 --> 04:07.118
But she can't receive a single yen, right?

85
04:07.185 --> 04:08.920
You looked into it. As expected from the police.

86
04:08.986 --> 04:09.954
-Ogoma! -Sorry.

87
04:10.021 --> 04:11.522
Anyway, thanks for the information.

88
04:11.589 --> 04:12.890
I'll give you one more thing.

89
04:12.957 --> 04:14.058
You can tell me later.

90
04:14.125 --> 04:15.660
-Hold up. -What is it?

91
04:15.727 --> 04:17.762
Ms. Tabatake’s daughter, Nono…

92
04:18.463 --> 04:19.997
has a rare disease.

93
04:20.798 --> 04:21.866
Rare disease?

94
04:21.933 --> 04:22.767
Let's go!

95
04:23.634 --> 04:26.571
Coming! Please tell me more later.

96
04:27.638 --> 04:28.740
Sorry!

97
04:30.541 --> 04:31.609
Sorry.

98
04:40.618 --> 04:42.320
Mommy is okay now.

99
04:43.121 --> 04:44.288
Don't worry.

100
04:44.355 --> 04:47.859
Please put on slippers and use hand sanitizer.

101
04:47.925 --> 04:48.793
Okay.

102
04:49.861 --> 04:50.928
I love you.

103
04:51.629 --> 04:52.563
I love you.

104
04:55.900 --> 04:57.201
Excuse me.

105
04:57.268 --> 04:58.503
Excuse me.

106
04:58.569 --> 05:00.438
I’m Awashima from the Shikara Station.

107
05:00.505 --> 05:01.472
I’m Ogoma.

108
05:01.539 --> 05:04.041
Nono, go back to your room.

109
05:04.108 --> 05:05.042
Yes.

110
05:05.676 --> 05:07.612
Sorry, we'll make it quick.

111
05:09.180 --> 05:12.250
VISITOR PASS

112
05:13.151 --> 05:14.185
It's okay.

113
05:23.161 --> 05:24.595
Sorry to bother you.

114
05:24.662 --> 05:25.496
Hello.

115
05:25.563 --> 05:29.033
Can you tell us what happened on the mountain?

116
05:30.034 --> 05:30.935
Yes.

117
05:33.204 --> 05:36.007
A tree fell when lightning struck, right?

118
05:36.774 --> 05:39.610
I told everyone to stay there for a while.

119
05:40.578 --> 05:44.515
We'll wait here until the storm stops!

120
05:44.582 --> 05:48.019
But Mr. Nikaido went down alone.

121
05:49.787 --> 05:51.522
You tried to stop him, right?

122
05:52.123 --> 05:53.691
Of course.

123
05:53.758 --> 05:57.161
But he wouldn't listen.

124
05:59.330 --> 06:02.600
While I was trying to deal with it, Ms. Saruwatari said…

125
06:02.667 --> 06:04.135
I'll go bring him back.

126
06:04.202 --> 06:05.236
What?

127
06:05.303 --> 06:07.338
I'll convince him to come back.

128
06:07.405 --> 06:08.272
A heat pack.

129
06:12.376 --> 06:13.244
What?

130
06:14.745 --> 06:16.581
Ms. Saruwatari?

131
06:17.882 --> 06:19.884
-She went after him? -Yes.

132
06:22.720 --> 06:25.923
As the guide, I should've convinced him to stay.

133
06:26.491 --> 06:30.261
But I couldn't leave the other guests.

134
06:30.895 --> 06:32.129
It's my fault.

135
06:32.897 --> 06:34.432
I'm sorry.

136
06:34.499 --> 06:37.768
Who prepared the food and drinks?

137
06:38.336 --> 06:41.372
Each guest prepared their own.

138
06:42.173 --> 06:46.377
I told them in advance to bring meals, snacks, and water.

139
06:46.444 --> 06:48.212
Even the late Mr. Nikaido?

140
06:48.779 --> 06:51.883
Mr. Nikaido was basically empty-handed.

141
06:51.949 --> 06:55.987
Did he eat or drink anything during the climb?

142
06:58.089 --> 07:00.992
I saw Ms. Saruwatari give him water.

143
07:02.627 --> 07:06.731
She gave him her own?

144
07:06.797 --> 07:07.865
Yes.

145
07:08.799 --> 07:10.468
Ms. Saruwatari

146
07:10.535 --> 07:14.372
kept worrying about him because he was unprepared.

147
07:15.306 --> 07:17.141
More than worried,

148
07:17.208 --> 07:22.013
she looked angry at him for climbing in light clothes.

149
07:22.079 --> 07:25.383
This pink flower is the pixie-eye primrose.

150
07:26.217 --> 07:29.487
-It has five petals-- -Please don't go ahead of the guide.

151
07:33.157 --> 07:34.592
Mr. Nikaido.

152
07:35.927 --> 07:38.095
Isn't there any place to get water?

153
07:38.162 --> 07:39.430
No.

154
07:40.665 --> 07:41.966
You again?

155
07:46.037 --> 07:48.806
Drinking it all before going down…

156
07:48.873 --> 07:50.408
I don't understand you.

157
07:51.342 --> 07:53.044
So you're not all bad.

158
07:57.348 --> 07:59.216
What time was that?

159
08:00.217 --> 08:03.220
During the descent. Before the lightning started.

160
08:05.756 --> 08:06.824
Around 1:00 p.m.

161
08:08.359 --> 08:09.393
Excuse me.

162
08:10.328 --> 08:14.865
Did anyone besides Ms. Saruwatari give him food or drink?

163
08:15.533 --> 08:16.567
No.

164
08:16.634 --> 08:18.369
Can I ask one more question?

165
08:18.436 --> 08:22.740
Before the tour, all five guests got hiking insurance.

166
08:22.807 --> 08:25.977
Do you know who the beneficiary is?

167
08:26.911 --> 08:28.446
Their families, right?

168
08:28.980 --> 08:32.149
All five had a third party as a beneficiary.

169
08:34.452 --> 08:36.721
Who is it?

170
08:36.787 --> 08:38.389
Aya Saruwatari.

171
08:38.456 --> 08:39.590
Were you aware of this?

172
08:41.459 --> 08:43.694
I had no idea. That's impossible.

173
08:45.262 --> 08:46.530
Could you have

174
08:47.798 --> 08:49.700
made a mistake on the tablet?

175
08:51.002 --> 08:53.371
A mistake like that would be a huge problem.

176
08:55.539 --> 08:56.674
Detective…

177
09:00.378 --> 09:03.714
I'm the beneficiary? Why is my name there?

178
09:03.781 --> 09:07.151
We heard you were worried about Mr. Nikaido during the climb.

179
09:08.119 --> 09:09.153
Yes.

180
09:09.220 --> 09:10.955
Why was that?

181
09:11.022 --> 09:12.356
Why, you ask?

182
09:13.157 --> 09:19.230
He didn't appear used to climbing, so I spoke to him a few times.

183
09:20.064 --> 09:21.666
Did you argue?

184
09:23.367 --> 09:25.069
No, it wasn't that serious.

185
09:27.304 --> 09:30.341
Did Mr. Nikaido run out of water on the way down?

186
09:30.908 --> 09:31.976
Yes.

187
09:32.610 --> 09:35.179
Who gave him water at that time?

188
09:36.147 --> 09:37.581
Ms. Tabatake.

189
09:38.416 --> 09:40.685
Not you? Ms. Tabatake?

190
09:40.751 --> 09:41.752
Yes.

191
09:53.764 --> 09:56.333
What are you investigating?

192
09:56.400 --> 09:58.769
We're just checking what happened.

193
10:00.638 --> 10:02.406
They're each saying different things.

194
10:02.473 --> 10:04.775
One of them is lying.

195
10:04.842 --> 10:07.812
Their statements don't match. Tell the station right away.

196
10:07.878 --> 10:08.879
Got it.

197
10:14.385 --> 10:15.486
Are you done interviewing?

198
10:16.287 --> 10:17.188
Yes.

199
10:17.254 --> 10:19.657
Then can I get their statements too?

200
10:19.724 --> 10:22.860
I need the accident details for my report.

201
10:22.927 --> 10:25.296
Did you forget the Hakodate case?

202
10:27.498 --> 10:30.401
That fake family suicide case.

203
10:30.468 --> 10:32.103
I handled it.

204
10:32.937 --> 10:34.271
What a surprise.

205
10:34.338 --> 10:36.707
How did you know it was murder?

206
10:38.776 --> 10:40.911
Maybe we're just looking at it from different angles.

207
10:40.978 --> 10:43.280
The police care about motive and evidence.

208
10:43.347 --> 10:46.517
I follow money. Only money.

209
10:46.584 --> 10:49.920
Your tip made the police lose face.

210
10:52.223 --> 10:54.125
Would you rather I hadn't reported them?

211
10:54.859 --> 10:57.194
The mistress who killed a family of four in a fire?

212
10:57.261 --> 10:59.296
-Should I not have-- -Are you picking a fight?

213
10:59.363 --> 11:02.933
If anything, you're picking one with me.

214
11:03.768 --> 11:04.835
Did it hurt your career?

215
11:04.902 --> 11:07.938
I'm now stationed in the middle of nowhere. Take the hint.

216
11:08.839 --> 11:11.075
Sorry, I'm bad at hints.

217
11:11.142 --> 11:13.444
-If you have tips, give them to us early. -Got it!

218
11:18.149 --> 11:20.751
Thank you very much for saving me.

219
11:20.818 --> 11:23.954
It was nothing. It was Ogoma who found you. Excuse me.

220
11:24.021 --> 11:24.922
Okay.

221
11:27.925 --> 11:30.828
Are you looking into Mr. Nikaido?

222
11:33.030 --> 11:37.535
Is there something suspicious about his death?

223
11:37.601 --> 11:41.705
I'm investigating, and so are the police.

224
11:43.174 --> 11:45.376
Let's talk casually.

225
11:46.277 --> 11:47.945
Where should I start?

226
11:49.013 --> 11:51.215
What's your relationship with Ogoma?

227
11:51.282 --> 11:53.083
Hello.

228
11:53.150 --> 11:55.653
The critical 72 hours have passed.

229
11:55.719 --> 11:57.188
What about the missing people?

230
11:57.254 --> 11:59.857
Ryutaro Monden, 30, office worker.

231
11:59.924 --> 12:02.793
His wife, Misaki, 31, housewife.

232
12:02.860 --> 12:04.795
Hitoshi Uematsu, 52, civil servant.

233
12:04.862 --> 12:06.797
-We already know that. -Their addresses?

234
12:06.864 --> 12:09.600
We don't disclose addresses or job details.

235
12:11.368 --> 12:14.905
Base to all teams! If you find anything the missing people may have left,

236
12:14.972 --> 12:18.909
including trash like plastic bottles, collect it right away!

237
12:18.976 --> 12:22.446
After that, ask the local station to help sort it,

238
12:22.513 --> 12:24.648
and send it to forensics!

239
12:24.715 --> 12:26.650
This is getting serious.

240
12:26.717 --> 12:29.053
What happened in those mountains?

241
12:29.119 --> 12:32.723
The three missing people weren't drugged too, were they?

242
12:32.790 --> 12:34.658
I hope not.

243
12:34.725 --> 12:37.494
Everyone, keep working while you listen.

244
12:37.561 --> 12:40.798
Tomorrow, support will come from Kitami HQ.

245
12:40.865 --> 12:43.968
They'll handle the interviews.

246
12:44.034 --> 12:46.003
We'll move on to canvassing the area.

247
12:46.070 --> 12:48.372
-Huh? -Mr. Awashima and Ogoma.

248
12:48.439 --> 12:51.108
Look into Mr. Nikaido's friends and security footage.

249
12:51.175 --> 12:54.044
Also, check the security cameras near his home.

250
12:54.111 --> 12:55.212
That's not fair!

251
12:55.946 --> 12:58.983
Let Mr. Awashima and me keep interviewing people.

252
12:59.049 --> 13:00.317
We are local officers!

253
13:00.384 --> 13:03.087
Interviews depend on experience.

254
13:03.153 --> 13:04.622
It's like pros and amateurs.

255
13:04.688 --> 13:06.323
-I have some experience too! -Ogoma.

256
13:09.627 --> 13:11.295
I'm 30 already.

257
13:12.963 --> 13:15.232
That's half my age, you know.

258
13:15.299 --> 13:17.268
How did your investigation go?

259
13:17.334 --> 13:19.670
What do the police think? Is it an accident? Murder?

260
13:19.737 --> 13:22.940
Their investigation is just starting!

261
13:25.376 --> 13:32.082
Even if it's murder by sleeping pill, it's very unlikely Harune did it herself.

262
13:32.716 --> 13:35.920
It will take time to find out if she was even involved.

263
13:35.986 --> 13:39.456
"I see! It takes time!" Did you think I'd say that?!

264
13:39.523 --> 13:42.726
Hurry and find Harune Nikaido and the people around her,

265
13:42.793 --> 13:44.395
and get the report in!

266
13:44.461 --> 13:45.663
Got it.

267
13:50.501 --> 13:52.169
Where do I go now?

268
14:03.914 --> 14:05.349
The funeral is tomorrow.

269
14:05.416 --> 14:09.019
We don't have much time, and I don't know where to start.

270
14:09.086 --> 14:10.654
Can you help?

271
14:10.721 --> 14:13.991
Also, how is that thing I asked you to do?

272
14:16.126 --> 14:17.094
Okay.

273
14:18.062 --> 14:19.163
Excuse me.

274
14:19.229 --> 14:20.064
Yes?

275
14:20.130 --> 14:21.365
Can I try this on?

276
14:21.432 --> 14:23.334
This way, please.

277
14:27.004 --> 14:27.705
Huh?

278
14:29.340 --> 14:31.742
Oh, my! What a coincidence!

279
14:34.545 --> 14:38.716
I'm sorry I asked you a ton of rude questions the other day.

280
14:40.117 --> 14:41.452
May I sit here?

281
14:41.518 --> 14:44.121
Of course not. I don't want to see your face.

282
14:44.188 --> 14:45.222
Excuse me.

283
14:47.324 --> 14:50.194
About the contract change two months ago--

284
14:50.260 --> 14:51.495
I don’t know.

285
14:52.763 --> 14:55.099
It was increased to 150 million yen, because…

286
14:55.165 --> 14:56.567
I don’t know.

287
14:58.535 --> 14:59.470
Well, let's eat.

288
15:01.839 --> 15:02.706
Delicious.

289
15:02.773 --> 15:05.042
CART STORAGE

290
15:50.854 --> 15:54.291
I'll be talking to your friends and acquaintances, then.

291
15:57.027 --> 15:58.962
Three people are still missing.

292
15:59.029 --> 16:04.068
We're stopping for today, but it has already been over 76 hours.

293
16:04.134 --> 16:07.304
Let's use all our strength to find them as soon as possible.

294
16:07.371 --> 16:09.006
That's all from base.

295
16:24.121 --> 16:25.656
Ogoma speaking.

296
16:25.722 --> 16:27.091
Can we talk now?

297
16:36.467 --> 16:37.935
Of course.

298
16:39.503 --> 16:42.439
Sorry for interviewing you right after your surgery.

299
16:44.408 --> 16:48.445
Did you misremember something? Mix some details up?

300
16:51.582 --> 16:53.150
Of course.

301
16:54.384 --> 16:57.387
Nikaido's death is an accident, right?

302
16:59.056 --> 17:00.824
We're still investigating that.

303
17:01.925 --> 17:03.227
Was he poisoned?

304
17:04.795 --> 17:07.764
No poison, no.

305
17:09.032 --> 17:12.169
Am I a suspect now?

306
17:14.004 --> 17:15.639
Not at all.

307
17:20.911 --> 17:25.649
We may ask for your help again, but don't worry.

308
17:29.253 --> 17:31.855
Do you need anything?

309
17:34.791 --> 17:36.059
A nail clipper.

310
17:37.060 --> 17:38.262
Huh?

311
17:40.464 --> 17:44.034
If you bring me one, it would help a lot.

312
17:44.101 --> 17:46.170
Okay. I'll bring one.

313
17:46.236 --> 17:47.237
Okay.

314
17:47.871 --> 17:49.606
Anytime is fine.

315
17:50.807 --> 17:51.875
See you.

316
17:52.743 --> 17:53.644
Bye.

317
17:55.846 --> 17:59.716
OGOMA

318
17:59.783 --> 18:00.984
Just ring the bell once.

319
18:01.051 --> 18:02.452
-Lend me your washing machine. -No.

320
18:02.519 --> 18:04.521
-Hey! -What?

321
18:04.588 --> 18:06.390
The coin laundry went under, right?

322
18:06.456 --> 18:08.859
Yeah. It went bankrupt before I came here.

323
18:08.926 --> 18:12.329
If you know that, lend me your washing machine!

324
18:12.396 --> 18:14.131
Wash it in the bath!

325
18:14.631 --> 18:15.532
Please.

326
18:15.599 --> 18:16.700
Today.

327
18:16.767 --> 18:19.469
Just for today. Please.

328
18:25.075 --> 18:28.178
Drink as much as you like. I don’t drink.

329
18:28.245 --> 18:30.847
I planned to finish investigating in two or three days,

330
18:32.549 --> 18:34.251
but it looks like it will drag on.

331
18:35.485 --> 18:36.653
Thanks.

332
18:38.422 --> 18:41.024
Can you tell me your info then?

333
18:41.825 --> 18:45.128
Why are you suddenly acting like a detective? What info?

334
18:45.195 --> 18:48.398
About Ms. Tabatake's daughter. She has a rare disease, right?

335
18:48.465 --> 18:52.169
Yes. The name is ECO deficiency.

336
18:52.236 --> 18:54.404
It's a rare immune disease caused by a gene mutation.

337
18:54.972 --> 18:57.874
Her immune system, which should protect the body,

338
18:57.941 --> 19:00.210
went haywire and now attacks the body's own cells.

339
19:00.744 --> 19:03.547
I see. What are the symptoms?

340
19:03.614 --> 19:06.817
In the active phase, the lymph nodes and liver become severely swollen.

341
19:07.484 --> 19:09.486
Normally, her fevers take longer to go down,

342
19:09.553 --> 19:11.488
and bleeding doesn’t stop easily.

343
19:11.555 --> 19:14.891
Well, if it gets worse, it can be fatal.

344
19:15.792 --> 19:17.594
Is she in serious condition?

345
19:18.962 --> 19:21.665
She seems fairly stable now.

346
19:21.732 --> 19:25.602
She's had a low fever for a while, so she's in the hospital, just to be safe.

347
19:26.703 --> 19:28.672
How can it be cured?

348
19:29.239 --> 19:31.208
It can't be cured easily. It's chronic.

349
19:32.709 --> 19:37.981
Gene therapy might remove the cause, and she can be cured that way.

350
19:38.682 --> 19:42.986
But they can't try it until she's more stable.

351
19:44.254 --> 19:47.491
For now, medicine to control the symptoms is the best they can do.

352
19:48.959 --> 19:51.762
Does the treatment cost a lot?

353
19:51.828 --> 19:53.830
You smell money too, don't you?

354
19:54.731 --> 19:57.434
But this disease gets government support.

355
19:57.501 --> 20:00.270
The cost isn't high enough to ruin your life.

356
20:00.337 --> 20:02.873
You talk about money a lot.

357
20:03.573 --> 20:06.877
Nothing shows a person's nature like money.

358
20:07.544 --> 20:10.314
Without even meeting someone, once I see their bank records,

359
20:10.380 --> 20:12.783
I can understand everything about them.

360
20:13.350 --> 20:15.786
If that were true, we police officers wouldn't struggle.

361
20:15.852 --> 20:17.254
Show me your bankbook then.

362
20:17.321 --> 20:18.188
Hey.

363
20:18.922 --> 20:21.625
Ms. Tabatake is a single mother.

364
20:21.692 --> 20:24.961
That's prejudice against single parents.

365
20:25.028 --> 20:28.065
-That's prejudice! -Do you think single mothers are all poor?

366
20:28.131 --> 20:31.335
-She's doing her best for Nono. -She even works as a driver on the side.

367
20:31.401 --> 20:32.536
Ms. Tabatake…

368
20:32.602 --> 20:35.205
She and Nono are doing their best.

369
20:35.272 --> 20:36.373
Sorry.

370
20:39.276 --> 20:40.177
Go ahead.

371
20:41.978 --> 20:44.081
I talked to the coroner who autopsied the body.

372
20:44.147 --> 20:45.215
You're fast.

373
20:47.417 --> 20:50.220
Who do the police think gave the sleeping pills,

374
20:50.287 --> 20:52.656
Ms. Tabatake or Ms. Saruwatari?

375
20:53.223 --> 20:54.658
We're still investigating.

376
20:54.725 --> 20:58.662
Who do you think did it, Ogoma?

377
20:59.229 --> 21:00.797
You tell me first.

378
21:00.864 --> 21:03.700
No. You tell me first.

379
21:03.767 --> 21:05.168
No. Here you go.

380
21:05.235 --> 21:06.269
Thanks.

381
21:06.937 --> 21:08.438
Okay. At the same time.

382
21:08.505 --> 21:09.639
-Ms. Aya! -Ms. Tabatake!

383
21:09.706 --> 21:11.575
Why Ms. Aya?

384
21:11.641 --> 21:12.809
By elimination.

385
21:12.876 --> 21:13.810
What?

386
21:13.877 --> 21:17.114
Ms. Tabatake earns money for her child's sake.

387
21:17.180 --> 21:20.884
Would a parent commit insurance murder for that?

388
21:20.951 --> 21:22.652
I thought about it.

389
21:23.220 --> 21:24.955
-What? -You actually think?

390
21:26.757 --> 21:30.627
Could Harune have given it to him when he left home?

391
21:30.694 --> 21:33.764
Maybe she gave him a slow-dissolving capsule or…

392
21:33.830 --> 21:36.032
I've handled cases like that.

393
21:37.000 --> 21:38.101
There's a delay, right?

394
21:38.769 --> 21:41.571
But the delay is only one or two hours.

395
21:41.638 --> 21:43.807
It wouldn't take until the descent.

396
21:44.908 --> 21:47.210
Then it needs an accomplice.

397
21:47.277 --> 21:52.115
Either Ms. Tabatake or Ms. Aya is the accomplice.

398
21:52.716 --> 21:54.451
The one who carried out the crime.

399
21:59.322 --> 22:01.958
I'm going to see Harune tomorrow.

400
22:02.025 --> 22:04.494
That woman never answers the phone.

401
22:06.430 --> 22:08.732
Your face… Are you coming with me?

402
22:10.667 --> 22:11.668
No.

403
22:12.335 --> 22:14.604
-I'm not doing the interrogating. -Why?

404
22:14.671 --> 22:16.706
I'm not free like you.

405
22:18.675 --> 22:21.445
Tomorrow, please tell me what Harune tells you.

406
22:21.511 --> 22:22.846
Huh…

407
22:22.913 --> 22:25.782
In exchange, tell me some investigation info.

408
22:25.849 --> 22:28.251
-No. -There you go again.

409
22:28.318 --> 22:30.787
I hate that about the police.

410
22:30.854 --> 22:34.357
They dig into everything about you, but give nothing back.

411
22:34.424 --> 22:35.859
I lent you my washing machine!

412
22:35.926 --> 22:37.494
I bought you beer!

413
22:37.561 --> 22:39.262
I haven't drunk it!

414
22:41.898 --> 22:42.933
Rain?

415
22:45.068 --> 22:48.672
The police stopped the search today because of heavy rain.

416
22:48.738 --> 22:49.673
Here's your meal.

417
22:49.739 --> 22:52.843
-They will resume when weather improves. -Your name, please.

418
22:52.909 --> 22:55.745
-Aya Saruwatari. Thank you. -Enjoy.

419
22:55.812 --> 22:59.749
Two men and one woman are still missing.

420
23:00.450 --> 23:03.353
In this accident, there has been one casualty…

421
23:03.420 --> 23:05.989
Ms. Saruwatari, you have a visitor.

422
23:06.056 --> 23:07.224
Now?

423
23:07.924 --> 23:12.329
We're collecting fingerprints from everyone involved.

424
23:12.996 --> 23:14.831
-Fingerprints? -Yes.

425
23:14.898 --> 23:17.501
It's voluntary, but will you help?

426
23:19.836 --> 23:21.371
Your hair is so messy.

427
23:24.074 --> 23:26.142
All right. Huh?

428
23:26.209 --> 23:28.178
You have terrible bed hair.

429
23:28.879 --> 23:30.847
I want another hair tie.

430
23:30.914 --> 23:32.148
Hair tie?

431
23:32.983 --> 23:35.285
Okay. Here.

432
23:38.388 --> 23:42.125
Dr. Yoshino said I could maybe leave the hospital with you.

433
23:44.561 --> 23:46.229
I hope you can.

434
23:46.296 --> 23:48.365
Excuse me. We're from Kitami HQ.

435
23:49.065 --> 23:52.135
We're here to ask about what happened on the 27th.

436
23:53.803 --> 23:55.639
Give me a moment.

437
24:04.314 --> 24:06.583
Were you acquainted with Mr. Nikaido?

438
24:06.650 --> 24:08.285
No.

439
24:08.351 --> 24:10.453
He looked kind of, you know…

440
24:10.520 --> 24:11.655
Kind of what?

441
24:12.322 --> 24:14.357
He looked shady, so I couldn't trust him.

442
24:37.247 --> 24:39.149
Hello?

443
24:45.555 --> 24:48.158
Is anyone here?

444
24:51.628 --> 24:53.597
Hello?

445
24:54.631 --> 24:58.301
Hey! What?! I'm scared!

446
25:10.413 --> 25:12.716
-What's wrong? -It's just…

447
25:12.782 --> 25:14.117
This car…

448
25:19.089 --> 25:20.323
Let's go!

449
25:20.390 --> 25:21.224
Okay!

450
25:29.733 --> 25:31.401
-No one is here? -Yeah.

451
25:31.468 --> 25:32.669
Let's go.

452
25:33.503 --> 25:36.439
-Shut up! -What are you doing! No! Stop!

453
25:36.506 --> 25:39.309
Shut up!

454
25:39.876 --> 25:40.710
Is it here?

455
25:40.777 --> 25:41.945
Should be.

456
25:42.012 --> 25:43.480
-Do you need anything? -Yeah.

457
25:43.546 --> 25:44.681
We're with the police.

458
25:45.281 --> 25:48.084
Does anyone here work at the restaurant, Orient Diner?

459
25:48.151 --> 25:49.719
Do you have an ID?

460
25:49.786 --> 25:50.720
You do?

461
25:50.787 --> 25:51.888
You do?

462
25:51.955 --> 25:54.424
-I'm Awashima from the local station. -Ogoma.

463
25:56.326 --> 26:01.064
We want to ask about the owner, Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido.

464
26:03.366 --> 26:04.901
What will happen to the diner?

465
26:04.968 --> 26:07.504
Did he act strange recently?

466
26:07.570 --> 26:08.705
No.

467
26:08.772 --> 26:10.073
-No. -Not at all?

468
26:10.140 --> 26:11.341
He didn't act strange at all?

469
26:12.175 --> 26:13.309
Does he hike often?

470
26:13.376 --> 26:14.310
He does.

471
26:15.011 --> 26:17.080
He often calls to say he's going on a hike.

472
26:17.147 --> 26:18.415
Who does he call?

473
26:18.481 --> 26:19.616
His wife?

474
26:19.683 --> 26:20.684
His wife?

475
26:21.351 --> 26:22.419
Or a friend?

476
26:23.620 --> 26:24.754
A friend?

477
26:28.058 --> 26:29.626
Oh, Liam!

478
26:30.627 --> 26:31.995
-Are they diner staff? -Yes.

479
26:32.062 --> 26:33.763
I'm good.

480
26:33.830 --> 26:35.198
It's the police.

481
26:35.899 --> 26:37.367
Hey! Wait!

482
26:37.434 --> 26:40.370
Wait! Stop!

483
26:40.437 --> 26:42.172
Hey! I said stop!

484
26:42.238 --> 26:44.174
Can we talk?

485
26:51.214 --> 26:52.282
Open the car.

486
26:54.050 --> 26:54.918
Excuse me.

487
26:57.220 --> 26:58.521
I'm going to open it.

488
27:00.657 --> 27:02.726
Calm down!

489
27:02.792 --> 27:04.327
Let's get you down.

490
27:06.496 --> 27:08.565
Okay. Ouch, that hurt!

491
27:08.631 --> 27:11.234
It hurts! Calm down!

492
27:11.301 --> 27:13.103
I'm with the police! It's okay!

493
27:13.169 --> 27:14.471
I'm with the police!

494
27:18.274 --> 27:19.876
It's you?

495
27:20.677 --> 27:22.345
-Okay. -I love the police!

496
27:23.246 --> 27:26.316
Okay, you're pretty strong. Let me go already.

497
27:31.688 --> 27:33.223
-Boss. -What?

498
27:33.289 --> 27:35.058
So it wasn't a kidnapping?

499
27:35.125 --> 27:36.192
No.

500
27:36.960 --> 27:39.262
I asked them earlier.

501
27:39.829 --> 27:43.233
They said Nao broke into their shop.

502
27:43.299 --> 27:45.902
So they caught him to hand him to the police.

503
27:45.969 --> 27:46.803
Sorry.

504
27:46.870 --> 27:50.340
But one of them had an expired residence card.

505
27:50.406 --> 27:51.808
He was staying illegally.

506
27:57.113 --> 27:58.648
Please say that in Japanese.

507
27:59.849 --> 28:01.251
Is the interpreter here yet?

508
28:01.317 --> 28:03.520
Hey. Wipe your sweat.

509
28:04.988 --> 28:06.689
You're making a mess.

510
28:10.126 --> 28:11.561
It's open.

511
28:11.628 --> 28:13.663
I hope we can go home soon.

512
28:14.464 --> 28:16.599
I'm fine with staying here forever.

513
28:17.267 --> 28:18.434
Why?

514
28:18.501 --> 28:21.104
I can be with you more in the hospital.

515
28:24.107 --> 28:26.976
When we leave the hospital, let's binge-watch Dandadan.

516
28:27.911 --> 28:29.045
And order pizza.

517
28:29.679 --> 28:32.715
Will we get the one with crab? I like that one.

518
28:33.550 --> 28:35.018
I like it too.

519
28:36.486 --> 28:37.687
What are you looking at?

520
28:41.424 --> 28:42.525
Officer.

521
28:43.126 --> 28:44.227
Yes?

522
28:44.294 --> 28:47.397
Would you like some pudding too?

523
28:47.463 --> 28:48.598
No, it's for your daughter.

524
28:50.166 --> 28:53.102
You can't eat two, right? Let's give him one.

525
28:54.237 --> 28:55.772
I don't know…

526
28:55.839 --> 28:57.240
Your call.

527
28:57.807 --> 28:58.908
Let's give him one.

528
28:58.975 --> 29:01.277
Are you sure? Then can you bring this to him?

529
29:02.412 --> 29:03.379
May I?

530
29:04.380 --> 29:06.916
I'll take it, okay? Thank you.

531
29:12.755 --> 29:13.990
Ms. Aya.

532
29:29.038 --> 29:30.940
-Yes? -We found fingerprints.

533
29:31.007 --> 29:34.544
From the bottle collected on the mountain, we found Nikaido's saliva

534
29:35.478 --> 29:37.247
and Saruwatari's fingerprints.

535
29:37.747 --> 29:41.017
Sleeping pill residue was also found inside the bottle.

536
29:41.084 --> 29:43.519
HQ is stepping in!

537
29:44.988 --> 29:46.055
Um…

538
29:47.790 --> 29:49.726
What about Ms. Tabatake's fingerprints?

539
29:51.027 --> 29:52.729
We didn't find any.

540
29:55.531 --> 29:58.701
It's now clear whose statement was right.

541
29:59.435 --> 30:03.773
Tomorrow morning, we'll question Saruwatari in detail.

542
30:05.141 --> 30:08.278
Am I a suspect now?

543
30:13.950 --> 30:15.551
You are.

544
30:24.794 --> 30:27.530
I saw Ms. Saruwatari give him water.

545
30:27.597 --> 30:30.500
Could you have made a mistake on the tablet?

546
30:30.566 --> 30:33.069
A mistake like that would be a huge problem.

547
30:40.276 --> 30:41.411
Laundry machine again?

548
30:41.477 --> 30:44.914
Thank you for saving my life today.

549
30:44.981 --> 30:45.949
Sure.

550
30:46.015 --> 30:49.018
-Know any places to drink around here? -Everything closes at 9:00 p.m. here.

551
30:49.919 --> 30:53.456
I want to show my thanks.

552
30:53.523 --> 30:54.691
Let me treat you.

553
30:54.757 --> 30:56.225
No need.

554
30:56.292 --> 30:59.062
Ogoma! You'll crush my head!

555
31:02.165 --> 31:04.467
I thought I would be killed.

556
31:05.034 --> 31:08.471
In that situation, I didn't care about money anymore.

557
31:08.538 --> 31:10.974
I would have paid everything I own to be saved.

558
31:11.040 --> 31:13.509
They didn't seem to want to kill you.

559
31:14.243 --> 31:16.379
They wanted to hand you over to the police.

560
31:17.613 --> 31:19.082
Did you do something wrong?

561
31:21.584 --> 31:23.720
I did nothing. Here.

562
31:25.355 --> 31:26.389
Thanks.

563
31:27.123 --> 31:29.192
Did you find out anything after that?

564
31:33.396 --> 31:35.965
I may have been wrong.

565
31:40.670 --> 31:43.873
About who gave Mr. Nikaido the sleeping pill.

566
31:46.009 --> 31:49.345
Was it Ms. Aya?

567
31:51.647 --> 31:52.749
We found fingerprints.

568
31:53.483 --> 31:56.219
What is Ms. Aya to you, Ogoma?

569
31:56.886 --> 31:57.787
Your first love?

570
31:57.854 --> 31:58.788
It’s not like that.

571
31:58.855 --> 32:00.456
-She saved me… -She is pretty.

572
32:00.523 --> 32:01.557
I'm grateful to her!

573
32:01.624 --> 32:03.359
I hear she's single.

574
32:03.426 --> 32:04.927
I'm just grateful to her!

575
32:04.994 --> 32:06.195
Ow!

576
32:06.896 --> 32:07.997
Okay, I get it.

577
32:09.465 --> 32:12.135
Since we're here, tell me about Ms. Aya.

578
32:35.658 --> 32:36.826
Hello?

579
33:05.421 --> 33:06.556
Nono.

580
33:09.559 --> 33:10.560
Nono.

581
33:13.930 --> 33:14.931
Mommy?

582
33:22.004 --> 33:23.139
I'm sorry.

583
33:26.876 --> 33:30.379
I'm sorry. I have to go home for a bit.

584
33:32.682 --> 33:36.085
The town I grew up in was dangerous.

585
33:36.152 --> 33:37.220
Where?

586
33:37.286 --> 33:38.221
Koura Town.

587
33:38.955 --> 33:40.123
Right.

588
33:40.189 --> 33:42.658
That town has assault cases every day.

589
33:42.725 --> 33:45.161
Everyone's parents were either ex-convicts,

590
33:45.228 --> 33:47.163
in prison, or addicts.

591
33:47.230 --> 33:49.031
Are you sure you grew up in Japan?

592
33:49.098 --> 33:50.433
-Anything you can't eat? -What?

593
33:50.500 --> 33:51.868
What foods do you hate?

594
33:52.568 --> 33:54.637
Like bamboo shoots?

595
33:54.704 --> 33:56.539
Give me some. Here.

596
33:56.606 --> 33:58.608
Our parents didn't keep a close eye on us.

597
33:58.674 --> 34:02.578
So some of us did terrible things, like assault, theft,

598
34:03.446 --> 34:06.382
or selling things washed up on the shore to the yakuza.

599
34:06.449 --> 34:07.984
-You mean seaweed? -No.

600
34:08.651 --> 34:11.721
Drugs thrown from smuggling ships.

601
34:11.787 --> 34:15.625
When the coast guard chased them, they threw the cargo into the sea.

602
34:16.792 --> 34:20.663
I saw some addicts naked, going wild,

603
34:20.730 --> 34:22.965
so I knew those drugs were bad.

604
34:24.534 --> 34:27.336
But in middle school, you want to try risky stuff, right?

605
34:27.937 --> 34:30.273
I only cared about entrance exams.

606
34:30.973 --> 34:31.974
Well,

607
34:33.176 --> 34:37.613
an older friend of mine said he found drugs at the shore.

608
34:37.680 --> 34:39.448
He said, “Let's try them.”

609
34:42.451 --> 34:45.955
In flowering plants, seeds are covered by protective fruits.

610
34:46.022 --> 34:48.391
While non-flowering plants produce naked seeds.

611
34:48.457 --> 34:49.625
Correct!

612
34:49.692 --> 34:51.060
I PICKED THIS UP COME, OGOMA

613
34:51.127 --> 34:51.961
Ogoma.

614
34:55.498 --> 34:58.201
I need you to help me with something after school.

615
35:00.336 --> 35:02.638
I thought I had been caught.

616
35:02.705 --> 35:04.173
Excuse me.

617
35:04.240 --> 35:06.509
Ogoma, pick this up.

618
35:07.944 --> 35:10.680
I thought, "Just say it already."

619
35:10.746 --> 35:12.949
"Report me if you want!"

620
35:14.517 --> 35:15.418
Huh?

621
35:16.085 --> 35:17.353
Bye!

622
35:17.420 --> 35:18.721
Now that I think about it,

623
35:19.288 --> 35:23.759
Ms. Aya was stopping me from crossing a dangerous line.

624
35:25.795 --> 35:27.663
She never lectured me.

625
35:27.730 --> 35:29.632
What about the kids who invited you?

626
35:31.234 --> 35:32.134
Were they caught?

627
35:37.139 --> 35:40.443
Two of them got caught and were sent to a facility.

628
35:42.044 --> 35:43.246
One…

629
35:45.715 --> 35:46.849
Hey, Tetsu!

630
35:50.353 --> 35:51.420
Hey!

631
35:54.056 --> 35:55.324
Hey, Tetsu!

632
35:55.391 --> 35:56.525
Hey!

633
36:09.672 --> 36:12.308
Hey, Tetsu, please! Wake up!

634
36:12.808 --> 36:14.710
Please don't die!

635
36:15.911 --> 36:17.313
Don't die!

636
36:18.714 --> 36:19.782
Please!

637
36:22.918 --> 36:24.320
Don't die…

638
36:24.387 --> 36:25.488
My friend…

639
36:27.056 --> 36:28.291
died…

640
36:29.558 --> 36:30.893
in front of me.

641
36:36.299 --> 36:38.100
He was like an older brother to me.

642
36:42.438 --> 36:46.175
I called an ambulance, and the police took me in too.

643
36:46.242 --> 36:48.411
You were doing drugs with him, weren't you?

644
36:49.078 --> 36:50.613
I told you I wasn't!

645
36:52.715 --> 36:54.083
Then why were you there?

646
36:54.750 --> 36:56.085
I couldn't reach him!

647
36:57.820 --> 36:59.889
I went to check, that's all.

648
36:59.955 --> 37:01.357
You did drugs, didn't you?

649
37:02.558 --> 37:03.426
Admit to it already.

650
37:08.064 --> 37:11.167
Honestly, I don't care how many idiots like you end up dying.

651
37:11.233 --> 37:12.668
Fuck you! I'll kill you!

652
37:12.735 --> 37:16.105
Go ahead. You're just talk. Don't underestimate adults.

653
37:16.906 --> 37:19.942
I'm Ms. Saruwatari from Koura Middle School.

654
37:20.509 --> 37:25.047
This boy was helping me clean the science prep room after school.

655
37:25.114 --> 37:27.283
It's no use, Teacher.

656
37:28.117 --> 37:30.353
These kids will grow up to be scum.

657
37:30.419 --> 37:32.088
Don't just assume that.

658
37:34.590 --> 37:36.992
There are things you shouldn't say to a boy

659
37:37.727 --> 37:40.329
who just lost his friend.

660
37:42.031 --> 37:43.065
Come on.

661
37:50.940 --> 37:53.743
We aren't finished interrogating him!

662
37:58.948 --> 38:02.318
You won't turn into scum. Never.

663
38:04.720 --> 38:09.992
It was the first time I felt that an adult was right about something.

664
38:11.827 --> 38:13.529
I see.

665
38:18.567 --> 38:19.635
What will you do

666
38:20.936 --> 38:22.204
if Ms. Aya is the culprit?

667
38:25.207 --> 38:27.510
If it's true, she'll be arrested.

668
38:29.545 --> 38:31.547
But if it's a mistake…

669
38:35.251 --> 38:37.353
I'll repay the kindness

670
38:38.421 --> 38:40.289
she showed me back then.

671
38:46.929 --> 38:48.931
You already saved her on the mountain.

672
38:52.835 --> 38:54.370
Not just her.

673
38:55.471 --> 38:57.173
I want to help everyone I can.

674
38:59.308 --> 39:00.776
Yes, Ogoma here.

675
39:02.578 --> 39:03.746
Understood.

676
39:08.918 --> 39:10.152
I drank the beer.

677
39:10.953 --> 39:12.755
What is it? Do you need to drive?

678
39:12.822 --> 39:14.190
-Going somewhere? -Yes.

679
39:14.256 --> 39:15.858
Where do you need to go?

680
39:15.925 --> 39:18.227
Ms. Tabatake has gone missing.

681
39:19.161 --> 39:20.296
Start with that next time!

682
39:22.198 --> 39:25.468
She left the hospital and then went to her apartment.

683
39:25.534 --> 39:27.169
Let's go there first.

684
39:28.737 --> 39:30.039
-Put it in. -Yes.

685
39:30.105 --> 39:31.140
I'll hurry then.

686
39:33.442 --> 39:34.810
Please do.

687
39:47.323 --> 39:48.524
Thank you.

688
39:52.194 --> 39:53.028
Ms. Tabatake!

689
39:53.596 --> 39:55.231
-Mr. Awashima! -Ms. Tabatake!

690
39:56.432 --> 39:57.600
-Get me the key! -Here!

691
39:57.666 --> 39:59.235
-Ms. Tabatake! -Please open it.

692
39:59.301 --> 40:00.402
It's open!

693
40:00.970 --> 40:02.304
Ms. Tabatake.

694
40:03.372 --> 40:05.107
Ms. Tabatake!

695
40:05.174 --> 40:07.443
Why did she leave the hospital?

696
40:23.459 --> 40:26.228
Ogoma! Ogoma!

697
40:26.295 --> 40:27.296
Ogoma!

698
40:27.363 --> 40:28.764
Why are you here?!

699
40:28.831 --> 40:30.666
Look up! Ms. Tabatake is on the roof!

700
40:32.601 --> 40:33.769
Please send backup!

701
40:33.836 --> 40:34.670
Roger!

702
40:44.780 --> 40:45.948
Ms. Tabatake.

703
40:49.018 --> 40:50.019
Are you okay?

704
40:50.085 --> 40:51.353
Please calm down!

705
40:53.055 --> 40:54.089
Let's go back to the hospital.

706
40:54.723 --> 40:55.891
Let's go back!

707
40:57.092 --> 40:58.027
Okay?

708
40:59.094 --> 41:00.296
Ms. Tabatake.

709
41:01.063 --> 41:01.931
Calm down.

710
41:01.997 --> 41:03.332
It's over!

711
41:03.399 --> 41:04.600
It's not over!

712
41:04.667 --> 41:05.501
It's over!

713
41:08.170 --> 41:09.371
I was so stupid!

714
41:09.939 --> 41:11.407
I'm also stupid!

715
41:13.175 --> 41:15.578
If you're in trouble, talk to me.

716
41:15.644 --> 41:16.946
Let's talk!

717
41:17.012 --> 41:19.281
We'll listen to your troubles.

718
41:22.952 --> 41:24.119
Ms. Tabatake!

719
41:30.859 --> 41:32.494
May I come closer?

720
41:36.365 --> 41:37.266
Is this okay?

721
41:37.866 --> 41:38.968
Don't.

722
41:40.903 --> 41:44.773
What do you call your daughter, Ms. Tabatake?

723
41:46.775 --> 41:49.011
Nono?

724
41:50.112 --> 41:51.647
Or does she have a nickname?

725
41:55.050 --> 41:55.985
Just Nono.

726
41:58.387 --> 42:00.255
So you call her Nono.

727
42:04.226 --> 42:05.194
Nono.

728
42:13.902 --> 42:15.004
Get her!

729
42:17.673 --> 42:19.375
Okay.

730
42:22.845 --> 42:25.614
I'm sorry. Did we hurt you?

731
42:27.750 --> 42:29.018
Can you stand?

732
42:29.084 --> 42:30.285
Are you okay?

733
42:31.887 --> 42:33.422
Let's go back to the hospital.

734
42:36.091 --> 42:37.459
I can't…

735
42:39.228 --> 42:40.362
Let's go.

736
42:41.397 --> 42:42.765
Hello, sir.

737
42:51.407 --> 42:52.841
Please use Japanese.

738
42:54.076 --> 42:55.377
Did you get all of that?

739
42:55.444 --> 42:56.879
I'm checking.

740
42:58.047 --> 42:59.381
You're okay.

741
43:12.027 --> 43:12.961
I love you.

742
43:18.133 --> 43:19.301
It's okay.

743
43:21.970 --> 43:23.439
I will settle everything.

744
43:37.586 --> 43:39.788
Ms. Tabatake! Stop!

745
43:40.522 --> 43:41.824
Ms. Tabatake!

746
43:45.594 --> 43:46.462
TRANSLATING

747
43:46.528 --> 43:49.098
They take people to hell.

748
44:07.449 --> 44:09.985
I have my sister's life insurance policy.

749
44:10.052 --> 44:12.821
Get a confession from Saruwatari.

750
44:12.888 --> 44:13.922
What do you think?

751
44:13.989 --> 44:16.525
Was it really suicide?

752
44:16.592 --> 44:17.559
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
